{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact 8d13c30af4eb2df95a3c22af4662864fd9cec761, all fourteen artifacts in corrected manifest af483840d21b50e556f2648ed3d139c9752f089c, primary 92561ab77732667fc56561e702c87fd87edbeeb6. Governed by #20424 / 1cb654fcee01c38a1f47996d82a2146de26e9e56; this closes review promise 9af4749e, not the implementation promise.\n\nSW-01 (blocking): byte-limited windows break cited-line selection and adjacent backward navigation. At internal/service/previewwindow.go@8d13c30af4eb2df95a3c22af4662864fd9cec761:84, the 400-line aligned start ignores the 64 KiB early close. Reproduction: windowFor([]byte(strings.Repeat(strings.Repeat(\"w\",1000)+\"\\n\",1000)),726,0) returns start401,end465 with no message; line726 is absent. Following Next on the same file returns1–65,66–130,131–195; Previous from131–195 returns1–65, skipping66–130 (line111 subtracts400). Select deterministic byte-and-line bounded windows that actually contain an in-range citation and offer adjacent reversible navigation, including the final window and out-of-range fallback. Keep the existing finite read/render limits. Add producer and real consumer regressions on variable-width lines, not only short numbered lines.\n\nSW-02: the whole-small-file fast path at internal/service/previewwindow.go@8d13c30af4eb2df95a3c22af4662864fd9cec761:64 ignores explicit start validation. windowFor([]byte(\"a\\nb\\n\"),0,9000) silently returns the whole two-line file with an empty message. Apply honest out-of-range handling consistently to small and empty files, retaining exact whole-file bytes for valid requests.\n\nSW-03: at internal/service/previewwindow.go@8d13c30af4eb2df95a3c22af4662864fd9cec761:97 truncation is recorded before the byte-bound check accepts that line. windowFor([]byte(strings.Repeat(strings.Repeat(\"x\",5000)+\"\\n\",100)),0,0) returns lines1–15 but truncated=[1,...,16], so the UI falsely says line16 is shown cut. Only name returned lines as truncated; test a truncated next line that does not fit.\n\nSW-04: ui/src/components/Preview.tsx@8d13c30af4eb2df95a3c22af4662864fd9cec761:120 splits exact whole-file bytes without following the server's line-count convention. Independent mounted React/JSDOM tests reproduce a rendered source row numbered0 under '0 lines, whole file' for empty content/window0..0, and rows1,2,3 under '2 lines, whole file' for a\\nb\\n/window1..2. Render exactly the real source rows while keeping the original bytes for Markdown. Test empty content, trailing newline, no final newline and actual blank final lines.\n\nSW-05 (validation): ui/test/preview-window.test.mjs@8d13c30af4eb2df95a3c22af4662864fd9cec761:59 does not exercise the claimed full review-link/history path. It mounts Preview with an already-constructed target, clicks Next, merely checks Previous's href, and jumps to the final window by assigning target. No opening review-link click, Previous click, reload or Back/Forward operation is tested. Add the existing routing consumer to the harness and exercise those actions; retain the separate exact-revision/cancellation tests and demonstrate that the relevant omissions fail. Do not describe a URL serialization assertion as browser history behavior.\n\nArchitecture: layers1 (Git reads) and7 (resident/API/UI) change the preview contract. The same head updates architecture.md and reading-view.md and all fourteen candidate previews are ready and byte-exact. The split 4 MiB verified read / 400-line /64 KiB /4 KiB-line design is documented, but this head does not yet implement the promised cited-line/adjacency/line-truth contract because of SW-01–04. Correct documentation to match the final window-selection rule.\n\nSecurity: inspected immutable verified Git-object reads, literal path checks, exact eligible revision/evidence ownership, same-origin bounded JSON, cancellation/deadline/concurrency, UTF-8/type refusals and inert React rendering. No new signing, custody, fold or completion authority is added. No independent trust-boundary bypass found; the observed failures concern content selection and truthful presentation. Preserve those boundaries in the correction. This is directly assigned implementation under #20424, not a new decision adopted through an authority-bearing request chain.\n\nSimplification: use one consistent window-selection/line-count rule for citation, forward/backward traversal and rendering; the separate fixed-400 backward calculation is the source of SW-01. PreviewContentLimit is now referenced only by the historical-ceiling test, so move that fixture threshold out of the production API or explain its actual supported contract instead of leaving a misleading live-limit comment. No second inspector is needed.\n\nIndependent validation: locked npm ci --ignore-scripts; tsc/build and make ui-check reproduce the committed embed; UI219/219; go vet ./...; fresh service and gitstore TestPreview suites (2.294s/1.150s); fresh docset gates passed. Four added Go counterexamples and two mounted DOM cases fail against this exact head as described. Full-suite Go and the eight omission reruns are not claimed for this rejected head and remain required for the corrected review. Local reproducible test sources and logs are retained at /tmp/git-window-review-{findings.log,ui-findings.log} and /tmp/git-window-codex-{review_test.go,review.test.mjs}. Requester should ratify this verdict, retain corrections on the existing implementation promise, publish the new exact head/current artifact set and request fresh independent review. No live reader replacement is authorized by this review.\n","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:92561ab77732667fc56561e702c87fd87edbeeb6","binding":"assigned","head":"8d13c30af4eb2df95a3c22af4662864fd9cec761","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:9af4749e0fec59df45fd310cefa9dd126ed8befe\",\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:af483840d2